>Another question on teleport and teleport-control:

>If I aquire teleport by eating a leprachaun I get randomly
>teleported away. So far so good. If I get teleport-control,
>still having teleport, I can control when and where I am
>teleported. But I am randomly asked if I want to be 
>teleported. Is this intended to be so? After all, it is
>quite annoying to be asked everynow and then 
>"Where do you want to be teleported", if I really do not
>want to be teleported.

>Any clues?

Yes.  Once you acquire the teleport intrinsic, the game will start to 
teleport you at random times.  Teleport control merely allows you to
control your destination when you do teleport, not when you teleport.
Also, high level characters with teleport can teleport at will by using
the ^T command.  If you don't want to teleport, type "." at the prompt
and you will stay on the same space.

